If the applicant is found in any illegal activity or any similar type of activity, then, concerned NEUTRAL CITATION R/CR.MA/23718/2024 ORDER DATED: 11/12/2024 undefined Investigating Officer shall have liberty to file an application for cancellation of bail against the present applicant.
In case of breach of any conditions, the concerned Trial Court shall have liberty to cancel the bail of the present applicant;
9.
The authorities will release the applicant/s only if he is not required in connection with any other offence for the time being.
If breach of any of the above conditions is committed, the Sessions Judge concerned will be free to issue warrant or take appropriate action in the matter.
10. Bail bond to be executed before the lower Court having jurisdiction to try the case.
It will be open for the concerned Court to delete, modify and/or relax any of the above conditions, in accordance with law.
11 At the trial, the trial Court shall not be influenced by the observations of preliminary nature qua the evidence at this stage made by this Court while enlarging the applicant/ on bail.
Rule is made absolute to the aforesaid extent.
Direct service is permitted.

